2
00:00:12,869 --> 00:00:21,289
<font color="#4096d1">本字幕仅供学习交流，严禁用于商业用途

3
00:00:22,165 --> 00:00:31,407
<font color="#4096d1">-=破烂熊字幕组=- 翻译: song123 校对&时间轴: tpring

4
00:00:36,072 --> 00:00:39,731
电视讲话

5
00:00:51,017 --> 00:00:54,009
汉弗莱爵士等着见您 首相
Sir Humphrey is waiting to see you, Prime Minister.

6
00:00:54,177 --> 00:00:56,532
谢谢 伯纳 让他进来
Thank you, Bernard. Show him in.

7
00:00:56,737 --> 00:00:58,807
是 首相
Yes, Prime Minister.

8
00:01:02,217 --> 00:01:06,495
早上好 首相      啊 汉弗莱 早上好
Good morning, Prime Minister. Ah, Humphrey, good morning.

9
00:01:06,697 --> 00:01:08,688
时差倒过来了没有?
How's the jet lag?

10
00:01:09,297 --> 00:01:14,769
我没时差...抱歉 我觉得我的时差是反的
I find that jet lag affects me more going the other way.

11
00:01:15,417 --> 00:01:19,195
我在白宫会面的时候感觉非常累
I felt frightfully tired at the White House.

12
00:01:19,195 --> 00:01:21,190
都不记得他说过什么了
I can scarcely remember a thing he said.

13
00:01:21,190 --> 00:01:24,775
他也没真的说多少 首相 他也很累
He didn't really say much, He was frightfully tired too.

14
00:01:25,657 --> 00:01:27,478
真让人担心是吧?
Bit worrying, isn't it?

15
00:01:27,478 --> 00:01:30,388
我们政治家总是满世界飞
Statesmen such as myself jetting all over the world,

16
00:01:30,388 --> 00:01:34,653
出席关于人类未来的主要会议 我们都累晕了
attending conferences on the future and we're zonked?

17
00:01:34,857 --> 00:01:37,246
有可能 首相
It would be, Prime Minister.

18
00:01:37,417 --> 00:01:42,411
也许就因为这个 谈判总提前由我这种下属完成
Perhaps that's why negotiations are done in advance.

19
00:01:43,017 --> 00:01:46,009
一般不留给晕了的人完成
They can hardly be left in the hands of the zonked.

20
00:01:46,697 --> 00:01:49,211
您找我什么事呢?
Now, what did you want to see me about?

21
00:01:50,777 --> 00:01:53,371
首相? 首相
Prime Minister? Prime Minister!

22
00:01:53,577 --> 00:01:56,853
啊 是的 伯纳 啊 汉弗莱 早上好
Ah, yes, Bernard. Ah, Humphrey, good morning!

23
00:01:58,897 --> 00:02:02,173
您想要见我的      哦 有吗?
You wanted to see me. Oh. Did I?

24
00:02:02,857 --> 00:02:05,224
你不知道他要说什么吗?
Don't you know what it was about?

25
00:02:05,224 --> 00:02:06,858
他还没跟我说就睡着了
He fell asleep before he told me.

26
00:02:07,377 --> 00:02:11,655
等有事我再来 伯纳 你有空了来见我
I'll be back if I'm needed. a word when you're free.

27
00:02:15,257 --> 00:02:17,248
啊 伯纳
Ah, Bernard.

28
00:02:18,457 --> 00:02:20,812
记得提醒我找汉弗莱
Remind me to see Humphrey...

29
00:02:22,497 --> 00:02:24,772
商量...某些事
..about something.

30
00:02:26,017 --> 00:02:29,726
我回来了 是不是有一大堆工作?
I suppose now I'm back, I've got a huge backlog of work?

31
00:02:29,937 --> 00:02:32,292
也不是 首相      不多吗?
Not really. No backlog?

32
00:02:32,497 --> 00:02:34,258
根本没事 首相
Nothing at all.

33
00:02:34,258 --> 00:02:38,936
当首相没什么事做 您已经没有自己的部门了
You have much less to do as Prime Minister. 

34
00:02:38,971 --> 00:02:40,566
伯纳 你不是说真的吧
Bernard, you can't be serious.

35
00:02:40,737 --> 00:02:44,095
对 您从报纸上读到的关于首相
Everything you've read about how hard a Prime Minister

36
00:02:44,095 --> 00:02:45,897
日理万机的话都只是传说
has to work is a bit of a myth really.

37
00:02:45,932 --> 00:02:49,014
照例都是新闻部发出去的
It's put out by the Press Office as a matter of course.

38
00:02:49,177 --> 00:02:51,975
不信您自己想想 您有什么要做的?
If you think about it, what do you have to do?

39
00:02:52,177 --> 00:02:55,169
主持内阁      一周两个半小时
Chair the Cabinet. Two and a half hours a week.

40
00:02:55,337 --> 00:02:58,454
主持两个内阁委员会      四个小时
Chair a couple of Cabinet committees. Four hours.

41
00:02:58,617 --> 00:03:02,610
一周接受下院质询两次      又半个小时
Answer questions in the House. Another half an hour.

42
00:03:02,777 --> 00:03:06,470
星期二拜见女王
Er... Audience with the Queen on Tuesdays.

43
00:03:06,470 --> 00:03:09,439
又半个小时      总共一周有七个半小时了
Another hour. Seven and a half hours a week so far.

44
00:03:09,617 --> 00:03:12,415
伯纳 肯定不止这些吧
Bernard, there must be more to it than that.

45
00:03:12,577 --> 00:03:17,571
当然 您得看所有的提要 我们安排您到处握手
You have to read briefs and shaking hands with people.

46
00:03:17,737 --> 00:03:21,558
可除了这些 有很多事人们期待您做
There's lots of things people want you to do

47
00:03:21,558 --> 00:03:22,624
很多事您应该做
and lots of things you should do

48
00:03:22,624 --> 00:03:26,768
还有些您能做 但是很少有事您必须做
and things you CAN do, but very few you HAVE to do.

49
00:03:26,937 --> 00:03:29,326
随您便 您是老大
It's up to you. You're the boss.

50
00:03:29,497 --> 00:03:32,011
谢谢 伯纳 我会考虑的
Thank you, Bernard. I'll bear that in mind.

51
00:03:32,177 --> 00:03:36,190
眼下 叫新闻秘书来讨论我的
Let's have the Press Secretary in to discuss my

52
00:03:36,190 --> 00:03:38,374
第一次首相级电视演讲
first TV broadcast as Prime Minister.

53
00:03:38,374 --> 00:03:41,214
请马尔康华伦马上来一下
Send Malcolm Warren up here straight away, please.

54
00:03:41,377 --> 00:03:44,096
我在美国很忙 极富成效
I was busy in America. It was a great success.

55
00:03:44,817 --> 00:03:47,285
是吗?      当然是的 伯纳
Was it? Of course it was, Bernard.

56
00:03:47,457 --> 00:03:49,519
你没看马尔康的报告吗?
Haven't you read Malcolm's report?

57
00:03:49,519 --> 00:03:52,745
我连着三个晚上在新闻上滚动播出
I was on all the news bulletins three nights running.

58
00:03:52,745 --> 00:03:58,463
"全景"的特写 1,269寸的专栏
Special feature on ''Panorama'', 1,269 column inches

59
00:03:58,463 --> 00:04:00,331
31张照片 16篇广播报道
31 photos, 16 radio reports.

60
00:04:00,537 --> 00:04:03,529
不是 那您取得的成就呢?
No, was it a success in terms of what it achieved?

61
00:04:03,697 --> 00:04:05,688
我刚告诉你了
I just told you.

62
00:04:05,857 --> 00:04:08,849
不 您和美国人的协议怎么样?
No, what about agreements with the Americans?

63
00:04:09,017 --> 00:04:13,488
您和总统的私人会谈 没告诉我结果
Your private conversation with the President? 

64
00:04:13,657 --> 00:04:17,126
对了 首先 我给他念了我的摘要
Oh, that. To begin with, I read him my brief

65
00:04:17,126 --> 00:04:18,775
他给我念了他的
and he read me his brief.

66
00:04:18,775 --> 00:04:23,331
然后 我们决定交换摘要自己读 可能会快点
quicker to swapped briefs and read them to ourselves.

67
00:04:23,497 --> 00:04:26,489
剩下大部分时间都在骂法国人
We spent most of the time rubbishing the French.

68
00:04:27,217 --> 00:04:28,536
真好
Terrific.

69
00:04:28,737 --> 00:04:30,887
好
Good. (PHONE RINGS)

70
00:04:31,057 --> 00:04:33,048
喂...? 哦 谢谢
Yes...? Oh, thanks.

71
00:04:33,217 --> 00:04:36,607
马尔康华伦马上上来 首相
Malcolm Warren is on his way up, Prime Minister.

72
00:04:49,017 --> 00:04:53,408
啊 伯纳 我们的首相兼第一财政大臣怎么样?
How's the Prime Minister and First Lord of the Treasury?

73
00:04:53,577 --> 00:04:57,456
正睡得香呢 爵士      伯纳 我们有麻烦了
Sleeping peacefully we have a problem.

74
00:04:57,617 --> 00:05:00,814
谁有?      你 我还有整个白厅
Who has? You and I and the whole of Whitehall.

75
00:05:00,977 --> 00:05:04,970
就是首相要命的新防御观点
The problem is the disastrous new defence ideas -

76
00:05:05,137 --> 00:05:09,130
取消三叉戟 恢复征兵 全是垃圾
cancelling Trident, reintroducing conscription

77
00:05:09,617 --> 00:05:12,575
宏伟蓝图?      对 他就是这么叫的
The Grand Design? That's what he calls it.

78
00:05:12,737 --> 00:05:15,900
如果能省钱 降低失业率...
If it reduces unemployment...

79
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:17,759
伯纳 我们国防政策的目的是什么?
What is the purpose of our defence policy?

80
00:05:17,759 --> 00:05:19,365
保卫英国      不 伯纳
To defend Britain. No, Bernard.

81
00:05:19,537 --> 00:05:22,529
是为了让人们相信英国受到了保卫
It is to make people BELIEVE Britain is defended.

82
00:05:23,537 --> 00:05:27,371
让俄国人?      不是俄国人 是英国人
The Russians? Not the Russians, the British!

83
00:05:28,337 --> 00:05:30,532
俄国人知道没有
The Russians know it's not.

84
00:05:31,497 --> 00:05:35,075
为了让我们天真 单纯的人民
It's for all our simple, ignorant people

85
00:05:35,075 --> 00:05:37,167
穿梭在家里 巴士和工厂
shuffling in and out of houses, buses, factories

86
00:05:37,167 --> 00:05:38,159
以及内阁的人
and the Cabinet room.

87
00:05:38,617 --> 00:05:40,972
国防是要让他们感到安全
We want to make them feel secure.

88
00:05:41,177 --> 00:05:43,353
但如果有更好的办法...
But if there's a better way...

89
00:05:43,353 --> 00:05:46,891
伯纳 我们有一个魔杖 叫做三叉戟
Bernard, we have a magic wand Trident.

90
00:05:46,891 --> 00:05:52,393
没人了解它 除了它要150亿
Nobody understands it, except it will cost ?5 billion,

91
00:05:52,393 --> 00:05:54,867
就是说它肯定很棒 很神奇
which means it must be wonderful, magical.

92
00:05:55,297 --> 00:05:59,176
我们只须签个支票 就都可以放松了
All we have to do is write a cheque and all relax,

93
00:05:59,337 --> 00:06:02,409
但是 如果政府里的人开始谈论
but if people in government start talking about it,

94
00:06:02,577 --> 00:06:05,091
最后 他们就会开始思考
in the end, they'll start THINKING about it.

95
00:06:05,697 --> 00:06:09,690
最终会意识到有问题 理论中有漏洞
They will come to realise the flaws in the reasoning.

96
00:06:09,857 --> 00:06:14,692
国家就会焦虑 动乱 怀疑 批评 最后改变
The nation will worried agitation, questions...change.

97
00:06:14,897 --> 00:06:17,809
改变?      改变
Change? Change.

98
00:06:18,017 --> 00:06:22,204
还有件事 这次电视讲话
There is one thing, though this TV broadcast.

99
00:06:22,204 --> 00:06:24,861
如果他要宣布他的新政策呢?
Suppose he uses it to announce his new policy?

100
00:06:24,861 --> 00:06:27,140
他不能 要通过内阁和下院
It has to go through Cabinet and the House.

101
00:06:27,140 --> 00:06:29,586
可以的 他可以引起全国大辩论
He can open the national debate.

102
00:06:29,586 --> 00:06:32,532
伯纳 只有政府下定决心以后才可能辩论
You do not until the government has made up its mind.

103
00:06:32,737 --> 00:06:36,252
如果首相打定了主意...      那他得打消
Prime Minister has made up his mind... He must unmake it.

104
00:06:36,457 --> 00:06:40,245
但是他是首相      是 确实是 伯纳
But he's the Prime Minister. Yes, indeed he is, Bernard.

105
00:06:41,497 --> 00:06:44,897
他有公派车 在伦敦有漂亮的房子
He has his own car, a nice house in London,

106
00:06:44,897 --> 00:06:48,222
乡间有别墅 无尽的宣传 终身养老金
endless publicity and a pension for life.

107
00:06:48,222 --> 00:06:49,372
他还想要什么?
What more does he want?

108
00:06:49,537 --> 00:06:51,971
我想他想要管理英国
I think he wants to govern Britain.

109
00:06:52,137 --> 00:06:54,367
阻止他 伯纳
Well, stop him, Bernard.

110
00:06:55,737 --> 00:06:58,126
是要访谈还是要讲话?
Should it be an interview or to camera?

111
00:06:58,857 --> 00:07:00,529
好
Yes.

112
00:07:00,697 --> 00:07:03,928
不 首相 你必须选一个
No, Prime Minister, it has to be one or the other.

113
00:07:04,097 --> 00:07:07,885
访谈怎么样? 伯纳 我们讨论一下电视访谈
What about an interview? we're discussing a TV interview.

114
00:07:08,057 --> 00:07:11,970
要罗宾戴 布赖恩瓦尔登 特里沃根还是吉米杨?
Robin Day, Brian Walden, Terry Wogan, Jimmy Young?

115
00:07:12,617 --> 00:07:16,132
你觉得哪个好?      得看您要什么形象
Which do you think? It depends how you want to appear.

116
00:07:16,297 --> 00:07:18,936
思想家 掌权者 人民的朋友 老好人?
The thinker, man of power, people's friend?

117
00:07:19,097 --> 00:07:23,852
都想 真的      他们四个不可能同时访谈吧
All of them They won't interview you at the same time.

118
00:07:24,057 --> 00:07:27,447
不 是我 我想显示所有这些特质
No, I want to be seen to have all those qualities.

119
00:07:27,657 --> 00:07:30,490
那好 那我想您还是讲话吧
Well, I think you should do it to camera.

120
00:07:30,657 --> 00:07:33,512
好 至少由我负责 不是那些
Yes. At least it'll be me in charge and not

121
00:07:33,512 --> 00:07:35,838
垮台的议员 高傲的主持人
all those failed MPs and jumped-up DJs.

122
00:07:36,617 --> 00:07:40,405
很好 政党宣言?      不 政党宣言会很闷的
Fine. A party political? No, spells instant boredom.

123
00:07:40,577 --> 00:07:45,970
我想应该是一个政府讲话 首相向他的人民演讲
I think it should be a ministerial broadcast

124
00:07:46,137 --> 00:07:49,129
但我要像政党宣言一样冲着镜头
but I'll do it into the camera like a party political.

125
00:07:49,337 --> 00:07:53,808
您似乎说过这很闷      我看他们讲很闷 伯纳
I thought they were boring. I'D be boring, Bernard.

126
00:07:54,417 --> 00:07:56,772
你觉得我讲会闷吗?
Do you think I'd be boring?

127
00:07:59,457 --> 00:08:01,448
闷? 您?
Boring? You?

128
00:08:01,657 --> 00:08:05,366
您常对镜头讲话吗?      不常 主要是访谈
Have you talking to camera? No, mostly interviews.

129
00:08:05,537 --> 00:08:08,811
那我最好安排一个彩排       好
Then I'd better set up a practice session.

130
00:08:08,811 --> 00:08:11,258
还有 这次讲话主要关于什么?
What is the broadcast to be about?

131
00:08:11,293 --> 00:08:14,527
关于什么?      对 是关于什么的?
About? Yes, about. What will it be about?

132
00:08:15,297 --> 00:08:17,572
关于我
About me.

133
00:08:17,777 --> 00:08:20,132
我知道 但是您准备说什么?
Yes, but what are you gonna say?

134
00:08:20,297 --> 00:08:21,889
说什么?
Say?

135
00:08:22,097 --> 00:08:24,088
对 什么政策
About policies.

136
00:08:24,257 --> 00:08:28,118
政策 是 我想就是些一般的东西
Policies, yes. I thought it'd be the usual thing

137
00:08:28,118 --> 00:08:29,939
比如 携手共创美好明天
go forward together, better tomorrow,

138
00:08:29,939 --> 00:08:33,046
勒紧腰带 齐心协力 治愈创伤 之类的
tighten your belt, all pull together, heal the wounds.

139
00:08:33,977 --> 00:08:36,730
是的 但您具体会讲些什么呢?
Yes, but what will you be saying specifically?

140
00:08:37,697 --> 00:08:40,086
哦 具体
Oh, specifically.

141
00:08:40,257 --> 00:08:44,773
我想我会建议我们具体的勒紧腰带
I'd suggest that we all specifically tighten our belts.

142
00:08:45,777 --> 00:08:50,293
具体治愈具体的社会创伤 懂了吗?
And specifically heal the specific wounds in society. 

143
00:08:50,497 --> 00:08:53,717
对 完全取决于您 首相
It's entirely up to you, Prime Minister.

144
00:08:53,717 --> 00:08:56,093
我只是在想 您要不要说些新东西?
I just thought if you had anything new to say...?

145
00:08:56,128 --> 00:08:57,609
新东西?
New?

146
00:08:57,777 --> 00:09:02,055
新东西 当然 让汉弗莱再来一下行吗?
Oh, new! of course! Get Humphrey back here, will you?

147
00:09:02,217 --> 00:09:05,926
我的宏伟蓝图 这就是我要跟汉弗莱讲的
My Grand Design. That's what I wanted to talk about.

148
00:09:06,897 --> 00:09:10,890
汉弗莱爵士 首相在安排他的电视讲话
the PM is making arrangements for his TV broadcast.

149
00:09:11,057 --> 00:09:14,572
他想谈他的宏伟蓝图 您能不能...
He wants to talk about his Design and wonders if you...

150
00:09:16,577 --> 00:09:18,056
喂?
Hello?

151
00:09:18,217 --> 00:09:20,606
我想他马上就到
I think he's on his way.

152
00:09:20,817 --> 00:09:24,730
宏伟蓝图?      现在不能告诉你 但是个大工程
Grand Design? I can't tell you now, but it's a big story.

153
00:09:24,937 --> 00:09:29,453
好 首相 我先找个制作人 安排彩排
I'll find a producer, set up a practice in the meantime.

154
00:09:33,211 --> 00:09:37,214
汉弗莱 真快      您想讨论一下电视演讲?
That was quick. You want to discuss a TV appearance?

155
00:09:37,377 --> 00:09:39,811
是的 但也不用这么急
Yes. It's not so desperately urgent.

156
00:09:39,977 --> 00:09:42,127
当然 确实不大重要
Not remotely important.

157
00:09:42,337 --> 00:09:45,488
不重要? 我的第一次首相级电视讲话?
My first television broadcast as Prime Minister?

158
00:09:45,697 --> 00:09:49,975
当然重要 但也没什么大不了的 不用慌
Terribly important, but not a crisis, not a panic.

159
00:09:50,177 --> 00:09:53,487
我想宣布我的新防御政策 你觉得如何?
I want to announce my new defence policy.

160
00:09:53,657 --> 00:09:55,648
不行      什么?
No! Pardon?

161
00:09:55,857 --> 00:09:57,927
这是个错误      你说这政策?
It's a mistake. The policy?

162
00:09:58,137 --> 00:10:02,927
当然 在这个问题上有新想法是很振奋
it's refreshing to have a new mind on the problem.

163
00:10:03,097 --> 00:10:08,091
挑战旧观念 质疑政府30年的思想基础
questioning the basis of government thinking for 30 years.

164
00:10:08,297 --> 00:10:11,289
你不赞成?      不 首相
You don't approve of the policy? It's not that.

165
00:10:11,457 --> 00:10:14,449
会有些牵连 反响 后果
There'll be implications, reverberations, repercussions.

166
00:10:14,617 --> 00:10:17,211
我们需要权衡事实 研究 咨询
We have to weigh the evidence, review, consult.

167
00:10:17,417 --> 00:10:20,614
你继续 汉弗莱 我先宣布了再说
You get on with that I'll announce it in the broadcast.

168
00:10:20,817 --> 00:10:23,377
您不能 现在还不能
You can't. Not yet.

169
00:10:23,537 --> 00:10:27,735
我们得通知美国人 他们会极力反对的
we have to tell the Americans. They will have objections.

170
00:10:27,897 --> 00:10:31,448
需要几个月耐心的外交
It will take many months of patient diplomacy.

171
00:10:31,448 --> 00:10:33,995
微妙问题要小心处理
Delicate issues need sensitive handling.

172
00:10:34,030 --> 00:10:37,170
汉弗莱 英国政府谁说了算?
Who has the last word about the government of Britain?

173
00:10:37,337 --> 00:10:40,249
英国内阁还是美国总统?
The British Cabinet or the American President?

174
00:10:40,417 --> 00:10:43,011
这倒是个有意思的问题
Do you know, that's a fascinating question!

175
00:10:43,937 --> 00:10:47,725
我们常讨论这个      得出什么结论?
We often discuss it. What conclusion have you arrived at?

176
00:10:47,937 --> 00:10:52,727
我是有点异端 我认为是英国内阁 但...
being a heretic I think it's the British Cabinet, but...

177
00:10:52,897 --> 00:10:55,286
我知道我是少数派
I know I'm in the minority.

178
00:10:55,497 --> 00:10:57,886
从现在开始 你是多数派
From now on, you're in the majority.

179
00:10:58,057 --> 00:11:01,845
我要向海外防御委员会提出我的宏伟蓝图
raise my Design with the Overseas Defence Committee,

180
00:11:02,017 --> 00:11:04,326
然后提交内阁
then I shall put it to Cabinet.

181
00:11:04,497 --> 00:11:06,965
我已经私下问过他们大部分了
I've sounded most of them out privately.

182
00:11:07,137 --> 00:11:11,130
他们都说能赢选票...极大提高国防力量
They think it's a vote-winner... a major contribution 

183
00:11:11,297 --> 00:11:14,687
我下午提交下院 晚上在电视上宣布
put it to the House, announce it in my broadcast.

184
00:11:14,897 --> 00:11:17,957
抱歉 首相 您现在还不能宣布
Sorry, you can't announce it yet.

185
00:11:17,957 --> 00:11:19,962
如果我不能 谁能?
Well, if I can't, who can?

186
00:11:21,697 --> 00:11:24,689
必须非常清楚地看到
So let us be abundantly clear about this.

187
00:11:25,297 --> 00:11:28,573
我们不能再透支了
We cannot go on paying ourselves more than we earn.

188
00:11:29,177 --> 00:11:31,771
世界上其它国家没有义务赡养我们
The rest of the world does not owe us a living.

189
00:11:32,377 --> 00:11:37,053
我们要准备做出牺牲...谁写的这个垃圾?
We must be prepared to make sacrifices Who wrote this?

190
00:11:39,897 --> 00:11:43,367
您自己 首相 是您以前的演讲
You did, Prime Minister. It's one of your old speeches.

191
00:11:43,537 --> 00:11:47,007
新的呢 电视讲话稿怎么样了?      还在打草稿
The draft of the broadcast? It's still only a draft.

192
00:11:47,177 --> 00:11:49,611
这可是排练      是机密
This is only a practice. It's confidential.

193
00:11:49,817 --> 00:11:52,968
这里都是自己人 拿来      是 首相
Everyone's been cleared. Go on. Yes, Prime Minister.

194
00:11:53,177 --> 00:11:57,170
如何 戈弗雷?      太棒了 首相 只有一点
How was that, Godfrey? Excellent Just one thing.

195
00:11:57,937 --> 00:12:01,407
您要戴眼镜吗?      你觉得呢?
Will you be wearing those glasses? What do you think?

196
00:12:01,577 --> 00:12:05,968
随您 戴上它 您看上去威严而果断
With them on, you look authoritative and commanding.

197
00:12:06,497 --> 00:12:08,931
不戴它 您看上真诚而坦率
With them off, you look honest and open.

198
00:12:09,137 --> 00:12:11,651
我想看上去威严又真诚
I want to look authoritative AND honest.

199
00:12:11,857 --> 00:12:14,325
只能选其一 真的
It's one or the other really.

200
00:12:14,537 --> 00:12:18,371
我可以先不戴 开讲的时候再戴
I could start with them off and put them on when I talk?

201
00:12:18,577 --> 00:12:21,489
这只显得优柔寡断      哦 明白了
That just looks indecisive. Oh, I see.

202
00:12:21,697 --> 00:12:23,892
单片眼镜怎么样?
What about a monocle?

203
00:12:27,497 --> 00:12:32,332
我们先不谈这个行吗? 能再来一遍吗?
Let's just leave them off for the moment Can we go again?

204
00:12:32,537 --> 00:12:36,212
新讲稿拿来了吗? 伯纳      是 首相
Have you got that new script? Yes, Prime Minister.

205
00:12:36,377 --> 00:12:39,687
三叉戟工程耗资太大
The Trident programme is too expensive.

206
00:12:40,497 --> 00:12:43,694
取消它 我们能省下几百万磅
By cancelling it, we shall release billions of pounds

207
00:12:43,857 --> 00:12:47,816
拨款以独特而新颖的方式解决国家问题
to fund an imaginative attack on the nation's problems.

208
00:12:48,337 --> 00:12:51,568
这个国家需要的...      能不能打住
What this country needs... Can we hold it?

209
00:12:51,737 --> 00:12:54,729
怎么了?      没事 很好
What was wrong? No, it was very good.

210
00:12:54,897 --> 00:12:57,570
首相...      等会 伯纳
Prime Minister... Just a minute. Yes?

211
00:12:57,777 --> 00:12:59,517
您能不能不要向前倾?
Do you mind not leaning forward?

212
00:12:59,517 --> 00:13:02,004
这样您看上去像卖保险的
It makes you look as though you're selling insurance.

213
00:13:02,937 --> 00:13:07,089
而且您会向上瞟镜头 像在哀求
it makes you look up at the lens like suppliant.

214
00:13:07,257 --> 00:13:09,930
您应该居高临下
You should be looking down from on high.

215
00:13:11,617 --> 00:13:14,973
好...这个国家需要的 这个国家需要的
What this country needs... What this country needs...

216
00:13:15,977 --> 00:13:18,127
这个国家需要的...
What this country needs...

217
00:13:18,337 --> 00:13:20,296
首相 马尔康和我起草了一份
Prime Minister, Malcolm and I have drafted a

218
00:13:20,296 --> 00:13:22,555
稍稍不同的讲稿      好
slightly different version to this speech.

219
00:13:22,555 --> 00:13:28,167
"我们应广泛考虑政府支出的各种选择"
''We shall review options over government expenditure.''

220
00:13:28,337 --> 00:13:31,329
伯纳 这太空洞了      谢谢 首相
This doesn't say anything. Thank you, Prime Minister.

221
00:13:31,497 --> 00:13:33,965
毫无冲击力      您太客气了
Completely lacking impact. You're too kind.

222
00:13:34,137 --> 00:13:38,050
不 伯纳 我不喜欢      您可以说"紧急考虑"
No, I don't like it. You could say ''urgently review''.

223
00:13:38,217 --> 00:13:41,687
不行      我真觉得应该缓和一点
No. I do think it should be toned down a bit.

224
00:13:41,897 --> 00:13:44,047
怎么缓 马尔康?
Any thoughts, Malcolm?

225
00:13:44,217 --> 00:13:48,608
"三叉戟是你们纳税人的重大负担"?
What about ''the Trident is a burden on your tax bill.

226
00:13:48,777 --> 00:13:53,089
"150亿是一大笔钱 应当谨慎审查它是否值得"
''We should see if it merits the ?5 billion it costs.''

227
00:13:53,817 --> 00:13:56,172
对 提到数字好不好?
All right. It's OK to mention figures?

228
00:13:56,857 --> 00:14:01,328
对 实际上没人记得 记得的也不相信
no one takes them in and those who do don't believe them,

229
00:14:01,497 --> 00:14:05,490
但这能让人觉得您对此了如指掌
but it makes people think you've got the facts.

230
00:14:05,657 --> 00:14:08,649
别忘了 人们不知道您是照提词机念的
People don't know you're reading off the teleprompter.

231
00:14:08,817 --> 00:14:11,809
没别的问题吧?      您念得有点慢了
Otherwise, it was fine? You were going a bit slowly.

232
00:14:12,017 --> 00:14:14,577
提词机走得就慢
The teleprompter was going a bit slowly.

233
00:14:14,777 --> 00:14:17,857
不不 它是跟您的速度走的
No, no. It follows your speed.

234
00:14:17,857 --> 00:14:19,729
试试先慢后快
Try going slow and then fast.

235
00:14:19,764 --> 00:14:21,892
哦 知道了      开始
Oh, I see. And cue.

236
00:14:22,057 --> 00:14:25,811
三叉戟...工程...是...
The...Trident...programme...is...a...heavy...

237
00:14:25,977 --> 00:14:29,970
你们纳税人的负担 150亿是一大笔钱
burden on your tax bill. ?5 billion is a lot of money.

238
00:14:30,137 --> 00:14:32,412
我明白了 真的
I see what you mean, yes.

239
00:14:34,777 --> 00:14:37,610
首相 能不能别说"你们纳税人"?
Would you mind not saying ''YOUR tax bill''?

240
00:14:37,817 --> 00:14:39,455
为什么?
Why not?

241
00:14:39,617 --> 00:14:43,974
听着像统治者在说被统治者 你们我们
It sound like the ruler talking to the ruled them and us.

242
00:14:44,177 --> 00:14:48,329
那我怎么说?      "我们纳税人"?您自己也交税
What should I say? ''OUR tax bill''? You pay taxes, too.

243
00:14:48,537 --> 00:14:50,302
好的 改过来 伯纳
Yes. Change that, Bernard.

244
00:14:50,302 --> 00:14:52,679
是 首相  我还是觉得太直接了
It's still very direct.

245
00:14:52,714 --> 00:14:56,768
谢谢 伯纳      不 很多人靠三叉戟吃饭
Good. No, lots of people's jobs depend on Trident.

246
00:14:56,937 --> 00:15:00,088
如果不经蹉商...      对哦 马尔康?
Until there's been a consultation... Yes. Malcolm?

247
00:15:00,297 --> 00:15:05,291
可以说"国防开支会受政府严格监督"
''Defence is one of areas we will look at closely

248
00:15:05,457 --> 00:15:08,893
"看能不能少花钱来达到同样的防御效果"
''to see if we can meet our needs at a lower cost.''

249
00:15:09,057 --> 00:15:11,730
太长了 能不能分成两句?      怎么?
Can you make it two sentences? Why?

250
00:15:11,937 --> 00:15:16,647
首相 我们发现一句话超过三行
we find that if a sentence goes on over three lines,

251
00:15:16,817 --> 00:15:22,050
等说到最后 多数人都忘了开头了 包括说的人
When it gets to end people will forget how it began.

252
00:15:22,257 --> 00:15:24,487
分两句 马尔康
Two sentences, Malcolm.

253
00:15:24,657 --> 00:15:27,410
而且您又向前倾了
And you are leaning forward again a bit.

254
00:15:28,177 --> 00:15:31,055
我是为了显得真诚
That's what I do when I want to look sincere.

255
00:15:31,257 --> 00:15:35,045
问题是 看上去像您故意想显得真诚
It makes you look like someone who wants to look sincere.

256
00:15:35,817 --> 00:15:38,889
向后倾点 看上去就很放松 很自信
If you lean back, you look relaxed and in control.

257
00:15:39,097 --> 00:15:40,610
就是这样
That's it.

258
00:15:42,417 --> 00:15:47,207
别这么后 那会像您中午喝高了
Don't lean back so far It looks like you've had liquid lunch.

259
00:15:49,017 --> 00:15:53,488
您可以在您想真诚的地方划线
underline bits of the script you want to look sincere,

260
00:15:53,657 --> 00:15:56,729
在那皱皱眉头 说得慢一点
then you just frown and say them a bit more slowly.

261
00:15:56,937 --> 00:15:59,007
还有别的吗?
Anything else?

262
00:15:59,177 --> 00:16:01,566
您的表情有点僵硬
Well, your face is a bit wooden.

263
00:16:02,097 --> 00:16:03,576
僵硬?
Wooden?

264
00:16:03,737 --> 00:16:06,205
对 只有说话的时候才这样
Yeah, only when you're speaking.

265
00:16:06,377 --> 00:16:11,167
一般演讲时 您会动动头 眉毛 面部肌肉等
In normal speech, you move your head and cheek and so on.

266
00:16:11,337 --> 00:16:15,125
别被题词机变成僵尸 好吗? 开始!
Don't let the teleprompter turn you into a zombie.

267
00:16:15,297 --> 00:16:18,653
国防开支
Defence expenditure is one of the areas...

268
00:16:19,417 --> 00:16:22,568
会受到政府严格监督
which this government will be examining closely.

269
00:16:23,217 --> 00:16:26,448
看能不能达到相同的...
It may be that we can achieve the same...

270
00:16:26,617 --> 00:16:30,610
停停 首相 有一点点过火了
Prime Minister, that's just a little bit too much.

271
00:16:33,657 --> 00:16:36,410
你们会听见反对党胡说八道
You'll have heard a lot of nonsense from the opposition.

272
00:16:36,577 --> 00:16:38,727
他们会说我们浪费钱
They say we waste money.

273
00:16:38,897 --> 00:16:41,730
他们会说我们巴结美国
They say we're selling out to the United States.

274
00:16:41,897 --> 00:16:45,094
我说 看看他们当权的后果
I say look at the mess they made when they were in power,

275
00:16:45,257 --> 00:16:47,976
看看他们对经济的破坏
look at the damage they did to the economy...

276
00:16:48,177 --> 00:16:51,748
打住行吗 首相 恕我建议
Could we hold it there? if I might suggest

277
00:16:51,748 --> 00:16:53,662
不要攻击反对党
don't attack the opposition.

278
00:16:53,697 --> 00:16:56,130
党内就爱听这个
Oh. Those are the bits the party likes.

279
00:16:56,297 --> 00:16:58,765
党内横竖会投您的票
Now, the party will vote for you anyway.

280
00:16:58,937 --> 00:17:01,611
您不能让摇摆不定的选民
You'll make the floating voter see you

281
00:17:01,611 --> 00:17:03,966
把您看成愤怒的分裂分子
as an angry and divisive figure.

282
00:17:04,001 --> 00:17:07,650
知道了 那我该怎么说他们?      提都不要提
I see. What should I say? Don't mention them at all.

283
00:17:07,817 --> 00:17:11,605
您所说的一切 都要让您显得热情友好
Everything you say has to make you sound warm

284
00:17:11,777 --> 00:17:14,575
威严 当然 也不失慈爱
Authoritative, of course, but affectionate.

285
00:17:14,737 --> 00:17:16,967
一国之父
The father of the nation.

286
00:17:17,137 --> 00:17:20,891
能不能直接跳到...新东西那里?
Could we just run forward to that, um, that new bit?

287
00:17:22,097 --> 00:17:25,646
尽量降低音调 好吗?
Try lowering the pitch of your voice. All right?

288
00:17:28,297 --> 00:17:30,686
我们要...
(HIGH VOICE) We want...

289
00:17:30,857 --> 00:17:34,645
我们要给子孙后代建设一个美好未来
We want to build a bright future for our children.

290
00:17:34,817 --> 00:17:38,332
要建设一个祥和繁荣的英国
We want to build a peaceful and prosperous Britain,

291
00:17:38,497 --> 00:17:42,285
能昂首世界民族之林的英国
a Britain that can hold head high in the nations.

292
00:17:42,457 --> 00:17:44,971
真不错 谁写的?
This is rather good. Who wrote this?

293
00:17:45,177 --> 00:17:49,807
实际上 是反对党领袖上次的政党宣言
it's the last party political by the opposition.

294
00:17:51,977 --> 00:17:54,650
关于您的形象 您要穿什么?
As for your appearance, what will you wear?

295
00:17:54,857 --> 00:17:59,055
你的建议呢?      深色套装代表传统价值
What do you suggest? dark represents traditional values.

296
00:17:59,217 --> 00:18:02,414
好 深色套装      而浅色套装看上去务实
Fine, dark suit. But a light suit looks business-like.

297
00:18:02,617 --> 00:18:05,814
浅色套装配深色马甲如何?
What about a lightish jacket with a darkish waistcoat?

298
00:18:06,497 --> 00:18:10,285
我觉得会显得您不知自己是谁
that would look as though you've got an identity problem.

299
00:18:10,457 --> 00:18:15,053
抱歉 首相 戈弗雷 能不能谈谈化妆?
Excuse me, PM. could we have a word about make-up?

300
00:18:16,737 --> 00:18:20,412
灰白头发行不行 要染黑吗?      不用 这样很好
Shall we darken the grey hair? No, it's fine.

301
00:18:20,577 --> 00:18:23,694
发际线后移呢?      什么后移?
And the receding hairline? Receding what?

302
00:18:24,217 --> 00:18:26,287
高前额
High forehead.

303
00:18:27,177 --> 00:18:33,491
能不能弄弄眼睛 显得它们不那么贴近?
And can you try to make the eyes less close-set?

304
00:18:33,657 --> 00:18:35,136
好的
Sure.

305
00:18:35,817 --> 00:18:38,285
眼袋打亮一点 脸颊上点色
Lighten the bags underneath.

306
00:18:39,537 --> 00:18:42,290
鼻子还是个问题      问题?
The nose is still a problem. Problem?

307
00:18:42,497 --> 00:18:47,332
不 只是灯光问题 首相 有个大...阴影
No, just a lighting problem. A very large, um, shadow.

308
00:18:50,457 --> 00:18:52,766
牙齿 当然
The teeth, of course.

309
00:18:52,977 --> 00:18:55,445
能不能笑一下 首相?
Could you smile, Prime Minister?

310
00:18:57,577 --> 00:18:59,215
对
Yes...

311
00:19:05,817 --> 00:19:09,492
首相 您想动个牙科手术吗?
how would you feel about a little dental work?

312
00:19:09,657 --> 00:19:11,932
拜托 能再来一遍吗?
Can we get on with this?

313
00:19:12,097 --> 00:19:14,247
好的 再来
OK, we're going again.

314
00:19:14,417 --> 00:19:17,011
太好了 开始 首相
Super. And cue the Prime Minister.

315
00:19:17,217 --> 00:19:23,008
我们应广泛考虑政府支出的各种选择
We shall review options over government expenditure...

316
00:19:23,177 --> 00:19:25,229
伯纳 这是先前那份
Bernard, this is what we started with.

317
00:19:25,229 --> 00:19:28,353
对 我觉得再合适不过了 首相
I do think it's the most appropriate.

318
00:19:28,388 --> 00:19:31,925
你觉得呢 戈弗雷?      这听您的 首相
What do you think? It's up to you, Prime Minister.

319
00:19:32,097 --> 00:19:35,089
我只想说 如果照这么讲
All I can say is, if that's what you're going to say,

320
00:19:35,257 --> 00:19:37,896
我建议穿时髦点 高科技布景
I suggest a very modern suit, hi-tech furniture,

321
00:19:38,057 --> 00:19:41,174
高亮度黄色墙纸 抽象画
high-energy yellow wallpaper, abstract paintings.

322
00:19:41,337 --> 00:19:45,489
全都旨在掩饰讲话本身毫无新意
everything to disguise the absence of new in the speech.

323
00:19:45,697 --> 00:19:49,485
我还是要用我爆炸性的宏伟蓝图演讲
I'll go back to my dynamic speech about the Grand Design.

324
00:19:49,657 --> 00:19:54,447
好 那就用传统布景 深色套装 橡木墙
Fine, then it's the traditional background, dark suit

325
00:19:54,617 --> 00:19:57,085
羊皮卷 18世纪的肖像
leather volumes, 18th-century portraits.

326
00:19:57,257 --> 00:19:59,646
还有 开场音乐
One other thing opening music.

327
00:19:59,817 --> 00:20:04,049
一样 巴赫配创新 斯特拉文斯基配保守
Once again, Bach new ideas; Stravinsky no change.

328
00:20:05,017 --> 00:20:09,533
我想选个英国作曲家 能反映我形象的
I think a British composer, something reflect my image.

329
00:20:09,697 --> 00:20:12,495
艾尔加(浪漫派作曲家)?      艾尔加 好 好
Sir Edward Elgar perhaps? Elgar, yes, yes.

330
00:20:12,657 --> 00:20:15,046
不要 "希望与荣耀之邦"
Not ''Land of Hope and Glory''.

331
00:20:16,417 --> 00:20:18,885
那"神秘变奏曲"如何?
What about the ''Enigma Variations''?

332
00:20:20,257 --> 00:20:23,169
他想说些激进的新东西
He's going to say something new and radical.

333
00:20:23,377 --> 00:20:28,132
又是那个蠢蓝图? 伯纳 明明要你避免的
That silly Grand Design? precisely what you had to avoid!

334
00:20:28,297 --> 00:20:31,050
怎么回事? 给我个好理由
I shall need a very good explanation!

335
00:20:31,257 --> 00:20:34,727
他很热衷      那和这有什么关系?
He's very keen on it. What's that got to do with it?

336
00:20:34,897 --> 00:20:39,095
事情不会因为首相热衷就实现
Things don't happen just because PMs are keen on them.

337
00:20:39,257 --> 00:20:41,771
张伯伦还热衷于和平呢
Neville Chamberlain was very keen on peace!

338
00:20:43,337 --> 00:20:46,135
他觉得能赢选票
He thinks it's a vote-winner.

339
00:20:46,297 --> 00:20:50,449
这就严重了 坐下 他为什么这么想?
That's more serious. What makes him think that?

340
00:20:50,657 --> 00:20:53,743
党派做了民意调查 似乎所有选民
The party did an opinion poll and all the voters

341
00:20:53,743 --> 00:20:55,443
都支持恢复兵役
were in favour of national service.

342
00:20:55,478 --> 00:20:59,569
再做个调查 显示他们反对兵役
Have another poll showing they're AGAINST it

343
00:20:59,777 --> 00:21:01,332
他们不能又支持又反对      当然能
They can't be for AND against it.

344
00:21:01,332 --> 00:21:03,949
伯纳 你被调查过吗?
Ever been surveyed?

345
00:21:03,984 --> 00:21:06,766
我没有 我家房子...哦 我明白了
Yes. Well, not me, my house. Oh, I see what you mean.

346
00:21:06,937 --> 00:21:09,735
伯纳 你知道的 一位可爱的小姐走过来
Bernard, a nice young lady comes up to you.

347
00:21:09,897 --> 00:21:14,368
你当然想留个好印象 不想犯傻 是吗?
You want to create a good impression, do you?

348
00:21:14,537 --> 00:21:17,529
不想      然后她开始提问
No. So she starts asking you some questions.

349
00:21:17,697 --> 00:21:22,293
伍利先生 您担心无业青年增多吗?
are you worried about the young people without jobs?

350
00:21:22,897 --> 00:21:24,216
是的
Yes.

351
00:21:24,377 --> 00:21:27,369
您担心青少年犯罪率上升吗?
Are you worried about rising crime among teenagers?

352
00:21:27,577 --> 00:21:30,569
是的      您觉得学校里缺少纪律吗?
Yes. Do you think our schools lack discipline?

353
00:21:30,737 --> 00:21:32,216
是的
Yes.

354
00:21:32,377 --> 00:21:35,847
您觉得年轻人欢迎权威和领导吗?
Do you think people welcome authority and leadership?

355
00:21:36,057 --> 00:21:38,207
是的      他们喜欢挑战吗?
Yes. They like a challenge?

356
00:21:38,417 --> 00:21:41,375
是的      您支持恢复兵役吗?
Yes. Would you be in favour of national service?

357
00:21:44,817 --> 00:21:47,285
我想应该是      到底是不是?
I suppose I might be. Yes or no?

358
00:21:47,497 --> 00:21:50,888
是      当然 伯纳 你说了前面那些
Yes. After all you've told me

359
00:21:50,888 --> 00:21:52,135
就不可能再说不是
you can't say no.

360
00:21:52,137 --> 00:21:55,766
他们压根不提前面五问 只发表最后一个
They don't mention the first 5 and publish the last one.

361
00:21:55,977 --> 00:21:58,286
他们真是这样吗?
Is that really what they do?

362
00:21:58,457 --> 00:22:01,767
有声誉的调查者不会 不过他们人不多
Not the reputable ones, but there aren't many of those.

363
00:22:01,937 --> 00:22:05,247
或者 这位小姐也能得到相反的结果
the young lady can get the opposite result.

364
00:22:05,457 --> 00:22:08,688
怎么讲?      伍利先生 您担心战争吗?
How? Mr Woolley, are you worried about war?

365
00:22:08,897 --> 00:22:11,411
是的      您担心军备竞赛吗?
Yes. Are you worried about the arms race?

366
00:22:11,577 --> 00:22:15,490
是的      您觉得年轻人持枪学杀人是否危险?
Yes. Is it dangerous giving young people guns?

367
00:22:15,697 --> 00:22:19,292
是的      您不同意强迫人们拿起武器吗?
Yes. Is it wrong to force people to take up arms?

368
00:22:19,497 --> 00:22:23,490
是的      您反对恢复兵役吗?
Yes. Would you oppose national service?

369
00:22:23,697 --> 00:22:25,176
是的
Yes.

370
00:22:26,617 --> 00:22:30,815
看到了吧 伯纳 完美的平衡样本
There you are, Bernard. The perfect balanced sample.

371
00:22:32,137 --> 00:22:34,385
所以 只要自己做个调查
So we just commission our own survey

372
00:22:34,385 --> 00:22:36,338
交给国防部就行了 交给你 伯纳
for the Ministry of Defence. See to it.

373
00:22:36,777 --> 00:22:39,769
好 那电视讲话呢?      他什么时候做?
What about the broadcast? When will he do it?

374
00:22:39,937 --> 00:22:42,053
下个月某天
Some time next month.

375
00:22:42,217 --> 00:22:44,606
告诉他得在...11天内
Tell him it'll be in 11 days' time.

376
00:22:44,777 --> 00:22:47,655
11天? 太快了 要是他拒绝呢?
That's a bit soon. Suppose he refuses?

377
00:22:47,817 --> 00:22:51,605
就说联合广播委员会透露
we've learnt from the Broadcasting Committee

378
00:22:51,777 --> 00:22:55,213
反对党18天后会做政党宣言
the opposition will hold a party political in 18 days

379
00:22:55,377 --> 00:22:57,766
他可以先做电视讲话
and he can get his ministerial in first.

380
00:22:57,937 --> 00:23:00,730
如果他想把任期内第一次政治讲话的
If he wants the first broadcast of his premiership

381
00:23:00,730 --> 00:23:02,592
机会让给反对派 随便
to be given by the opposition, fine.

382
00:23:04,057 --> 00:23:06,287
这是真的吗?
Erm, is that true?

383
00:23:06,497 --> 00:23:10,490
会是的 如果你明早之前不提的话
It will be... if you don't mention it till tomorrow.

384
00:23:10,697 --> 00:23:14,167
他还是可以宣布新政策      我想不会
He could still announce his new policy. I don't think so.

385
00:23:14,337 --> 00:23:17,454
他和内阁同僚只有一次会议机会
He'll have only one meeting with his Cabinet colleagues.

386
00:23:17,657 --> 00:23:19,852
内阁同僚们都支持这个政策
They're all in favour of it.

387
00:23:20,057 --> 00:23:22,048
那只是私下的 政见上的
Only personally and politically

388
00:23:22,048 --> 00:23:26,126
作为各部大臣 他们正式支持吗?
but are they in favour as departmental ministers?

389
00:23:26,161 --> 00:23:28,894
懂了 这取决于他们得到的建议?
I see. That will depend on the advice they get.

390
00:23:33,177 --> 00:23:39,332
当然 我知道 我们从原则上支持他取消三叉戟
there's no question of our opposing cancel Trident.

391
00:23:39,537 --> 00:23:44,531
问题在于 考虑到一切后果之前应该缓行
It's holding back until we've through the implications.

392
00:23:44,697 --> 00:23:48,576
说说 你准备怎么告诉你的就业大臣?
So what are you going to brief your man at Employment?

393
00:23:48,777 --> 00:23:51,132
其他人怎么说?
What are the others saying?

394
00:23:51,297 --> 00:23:55,290
迪克会告诉外交大臣说美国很生气?
Will Dick brief the FS the Americans will hit the roof?

395
00:23:55,457 --> 00:23:58,255
不 他觉得更有力的说法是
No, he thinks it might be more persuasive

396
00:23:58,417 --> 00:24:03,571
取消三叉戟显得软弱 姑息苏联
to argue that cancelling Trident will look like weakness,

397
00:24:04,257 --> 00:24:06,248
好想法
Good thinking.

398
00:24:06,417 --> 00:24:08,885
就像诺曼不会告诉他的国防大臣
Just as Norman won't tell his man at Defence

399
00:24:09,057 --> 00:24:13,767
三军不乐意精锐部队里充斥小流氓
service chiefs won't have elite diluted with riff-raff.

400
00:24:13,937 --> 00:24:17,896
他们是不乐意      他觉得需要别的理由
But they won't? He felt they needed another argument.

401
00:24:18,097 --> 00:24:24,286
两个理由? 这也太压迫国防大臣...
Two? Isn't that putting a strain on the DS's somewhat...

402
00:24:24,497 --> 00:24:27,773
生锈的头脑? 是的
Obsolete intellectual equipment? Yes.

403
00:24:29,417 --> 00:24:32,350
他只会说 三叉戟是最好的
He's just going to brief him that Trident is best

404
00:24:32,350 --> 00:24:34,158
英国得拥有最好的
and Britain must have the best.

405
00:24:34,193 --> 00:24:38,568
好 就算国防部长也该理解这个
Even the Defence Secretary should be able to handle that.

406
00:24:38,777 --> 00:24:41,166
只要稍稍点拨一下 是的
With a bit of coaching, yes.

407
00:24:41,337 --> 00:24:43,328
盖尔呢? 我知道了
And Giles? I know!

408
00:24:43,497 --> 00:24:48,287
教师工会很害怕 征兵会暴露
The Union of Teachers are scared that conscription will expose

409
00:24:48,457 --> 00:24:53,531
毕业生尽管擅长社交和自我表现
that school leavers integrated socially and aware...

410
00:24:53,737 --> 00:24:56,729
却连读写算都不会 对
Can't actually read, write or do sums, yes.

411
00:24:58,017 --> 00:25:00,485
盖尔让教育大臣担心
Giles has got the Education Secretary worried

412
00:25:00,657 --> 00:25:05,128
大学更乐于让军方接收一些学校
that their education is to be taken over by the services

413
00:25:05,297 --> 00:25:07,765
用来教书育人
and actually used for teaching people.

414
00:25:08,857 --> 00:25:13,214
那可不行     不行 你就业部那位呢?
We can't have that. So what about your man at Employment?

415
00:25:13,377 --> 00:25:15,447
一样的
It's the same problem.

416
00:25:15,617 --> 00:25:19,895
说实话 工会无法忍受被小孩抢走社区工作
the unions don't want kids undercutting them on work.

417
00:25:20,097 --> 00:25:21,416
是的
Yes.

418
00:25:21,577 --> 00:25:24,967
我觉得这个阶段用不上事实
I don't think we need to bring the truth at this stage.

419
00:25:26,657 --> 00:25:28,454
等等
Hold on.

420
00:25:29,057 --> 00:25:31,287
假设他说
Now, suppose he argues

421
00:25:31,457 --> 00:25:34,529
眼下的无业青年
that unemployed young people are, at the moment,

422
00:25:34,697 --> 00:25:37,848
不健康 无训练 无组织 无纪律
unfit, unorganised, undisciplined and untrained,

423
00:25:38,017 --> 00:25:42,772
但征兵最终会释放满大街
but that conscription will release on to the streets

424
00:25:42,937 --> 00:25:46,691
健壮 擅长杀戮的青年军人
an army of fit young people, all trained to kill.

425
00:25:47,337 --> 00:25:49,328
说得好
Good man!

426
00:25:50,097 --> 00:25:52,486
他真会相信吗?
Does he actually believe that?

427
00:25:52,657 --> 00:25:55,046
会的 明天早上之前
He will by tomorrow morning.

428
00:25:57,537 --> 00:25:59,528
啊 汉弗莱
Ah, Humphrey.

429
00:25:59,697 --> 00:26:01,688
先生们 借过
Gentlemen. Sorry.

430
00:26:03,177 --> 00:26:05,168
会开得如何 首相?
Good committee, Prime Minister?

431
00:26:05,337 --> 00:26:08,249
奇怪 奇怪      怎么个奇怪法?
Extraordinary. Extraordinary. How extraordinary?

432
00:26:08,457 --> 00:26:11,927
上星期 所有同僚都赞成我的宏伟蓝图
Last week, all my colleagues were for my Grand Design.

433
00:26:12,097 --> 00:26:13,769
现在呢?
And now?

434
00:26:13,937 --> 00:26:16,929
外交大臣说这是向俄国低头
The Foreign Secretary says it would appease the Soviets.

435
00:26:17,097 --> 00:26:19,486
真没想到会这样
I hadn't thought of that.

436
00:26:19,697 --> 00:26:22,441
国防大臣说 三叉戟是最好的
The Defence Secretary says Trident is best

437
00:26:22,441 --> 00:26:24,241
英国就得有最好的
and Britain must have the best.

438
00:26:24,241 --> 00:26:26,576
他真这么说? 真奇怪
Does he really? How fascinating!

439
00:26:27,297 --> 00:26:32,087
教育大臣说征兵会破坏教育系统
The Education says it would undermine the system.

440
00:26:32,257 --> 00:26:35,010
是个问题 就业大臣呢?
It is a worry. And the Employment Secretary?

441
00:26:35,217 --> 00:26:39,347
他说不能把一百万训练有素的
he goes on about a million unemployed trained fighters

442
00:26:39,347 --> 00:26:41,047
失业战士放到大街上
being let loose on the streets.

443
00:26:41,857 --> 00:26:45,247
是有点道理      我就想不通了
Well, he has a point there. I don't understand it.

444
00:26:45,417 --> 00:26:48,179
上星期他们还说 新国防政策
Last week, they all thought my new defence policy

445
00:26:48,179 --> 00:26:51,345
会受欢迎的 你能解释吗 汉弗莱?
was a winner. Can you explain it?

446
00:26:51,345 --> 00:26:53,485
我能力有限 首相 什么 伯纳?
It's beyond me, Prime Minister. Yes, Bernard?

447
00:26:53,657 --> 00:26:57,286
打扰一下 首相 国防部说很紧急
Sorry to interrupt, PM. The MoD said it was urgent.

448
00:26:59,137 --> 00:27:00,490
什么?
What?

449
00:27:00,697 --> 00:27:04,485
好像有74%的群众反对征兵
74% of the population are against conscription.

450
00:27:06,297 --> 00:27:08,731
74...? 天哪
74...? Good Lord!

451
00:27:10,817 --> 00:27:14,253
上次党派的调查说有63%的人支持
The party poll said 63% of the population was for it.

452
00:27:15,777 --> 00:27:19,326
您看 党派的数据很不可靠 首相
party figures can be very unreliable, Prime Minister.

453
00:27:19,497 --> 00:27:22,250
可不是      我提议用折中方案
Evidently. May I suggest a compromise?

454
00:27:23,177 --> 00:27:28,171
显然 委员会认为您的新政策非常好
the committee's agreed that your new policy is excellent

455
00:27:28,337 --> 00:27:30,805
但是基于刚才说到的担心
but in view of some of the doubts expressed,

456
00:27:30,977 --> 00:27:35,971
我认为委员会的意思是 经过再三考虑
may I propose that the view of the committee was

457
00:27:36,137 --> 00:27:39,527
尽管提案纲领得到广泛认可
while the proposal met with broad approval in principle,

458
00:27:39,697 --> 00:27:43,485
某些原则理论原则上可行
some of the principles were fundamental in principle

459
00:27:43,657 --> 00:27:47,855
某些方面太复杂 在实践中需要微妙的平衡
and some of the considerations balanced in practice

460
00:27:48,017 --> 00:27:52,135
所以原则上 明智谨慎的方案
it was proposed that the sensible and prudent practice

461
00:27:52,297 --> 00:27:56,085
只有将提案付诸更加详细的考虑
would be to submit the proposal for consideration,

462
00:27:56,257 --> 00:28:00,648
加强新提案和已有原则的连续性
stressing the continuity of the proposal with principles

463
00:28:00,817 --> 00:28:03,285
以及原则的原则性争论
and the principle of the principal arguments

464
00:28:03,457 --> 00:28:07,928
由提议者在提议中建议批准的 从原则上
which the proposer proposes for approval in principle.

465
00:28:09,337 --> 00:28:10,895
什么?
What?

466
00:28:11,097 --> 00:28:15,136
不要在周五电视讲话上提您的宏伟蓝图
Don't refer to your Grand Design in your broadcast

467
00:28:15,817 --> 00:28:19,412
你不是建议我放弃吧      天哪 不是
You're not suggesting I should abandon it? no!

468
00:28:19,577 --> 00:28:22,045
千万别 这是绝妙的政策
Heaven forbid! It is a most excellent policy!

469
00:28:22,697 --> 00:28:26,485
好吧 我先深入了解一阵再宣布
We'll look into it further before I say anything

470
00:28:26,697 --> 00:28:31,566
首相 电视台要敲定讲话的背景
TV want a decision about the background for broadcast.

471
00:28:31,737 --> 00:28:34,307
还是时髦服装 高科技布景
better be the modern suit with the hi-tech furniture

472
00:28:34,307 --> 00:28:37,961
和高亮黄色墙纸吧
and the yellow wallpaper.

473
00:28:37,996 --> 00:28:39,927
还有抽象画?
And abstract paintings?

474
00:28:40,137 --> 00:28:42,731
得要吧 还有斯特拉文斯基?
I suppose so. And Stravinsky?

475
00:28:42,937 --> 00:28:45,405
是 首相
Yes, Prime Minister.

476
00:28:47,372 --> 00:28:57,867
